    explain: "Both services carry a WAF and the difference is reach: <b>Front Door</b> is <b>global</b> — it comes in when there are several regions, worldwide latency or failover — and <b>Application Gateway</b> is <b>regional</b>, inside the virtual network, for when traffic must not leave it. Azure Firewall filters network and protocol, not HTTP requests. And a network security group opens ports: it does not look at content. <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/web-application-firewall/afds/afds-overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Microsoft Learn ↗</a>",
