    explain: "The secure score is a <b>generic prioritised guide</b>: it weights each action by the impact it typically has on an average organisation, not by what is happening to this one. Chasing points can mean implementing controls of little value to their actual estate while leaving undone the one that closes their specific vector, which may be worth few points. Use it as an input, crossed with their own threat model and with whatever exposure management flags as a real attack path. 90% is not impossible by definition, points do not correlate with cost, and whole categories need not be completed. <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/defender-xdr/microsoft-secure-score\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Microsoft Learn ↗</a>",
